From c368376f605f9d1301bb3758f44b17dd5967185d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (SGR dev session)" <claude@sgr-dev.local>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 08:28:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(risk): add extended Startup Safety Checks (Phase 2 -
 live trading safety, Baustein 5)

- Add sgr/core/startup_checks.py: StartupSafetyChecker, run fail-fast
  before any connection (DB, Redis, Exchange) is established. Distinct
  from SGRConfig.validate_production_constraints() (secret/debug defaults
  at config-load time) and the per-request confirm_live guard in
  api/routers/trading.py (protects the manual trading-cycle endpoint) -
  this protects the boot itself, unconditionally.
  Checks:
    - kill_switch_not_preactivated (all modes): kill switch for the
      active trading mode must not already be triggered at boot.
    - live_credentials_present (LIVE only): reuses the existing, already
      tested ExchangeCredentials.get_credentials() validation, fails
      early instead of at first exchange connect attempt.
    - risk_limits_not_disabled (LIVE only): max_portfolio_drawdown and
      daily_loss_limit must not sit at the permissive ceiling of their
      allowed Pydantic range.
    - max_leverage_sane (LIVE only): max_leverage must not exceed a sane
      10x ceiling, which would make the Baustein-2 Leverage Guard
      practically useless.
    - max_order_notional_sane (LIVE only): max_order_notional (Baustein 4)
      must not be disabled (None) in LIVE mode.
  run() collects all check results (does not stop at first failure) so a
  misconfiguration surfaces completely in a single StartupSafetyError.
- Wire into sgr/api/main.py lifespan as new step 1a, immediately after
  logging setup and before observability/DB/exchange init.
- tests/api/test_main.py: patch StartupSafetyChecker.run_or_raise as a
  no-op in _patch_lifespan_dependencies, since those tests use a
  MagicMock config (not a real SGRConfig) and exist to cover lifespan
  infrastructure wiring, not safety-check logic (which has its own
  dedicated test file).
- New tests/unit/test_startup_checks.py: 23 tests covering every check
  individually plus run_or_raise() integration behavior (exception type,
  multi-failure aggregation, PAPER mode skipping LIVE-only checks).
- Full suite verified green: 1316 passed (was 1293), 9 skipped, 0 failed.
  Coverage 94.15% -> 94.21%. sgr/core/startup_checks.py: 100%.
  sgr/api/main.py: 100% (unchanged). ruff unchanged (22, pre-existing).
  mypy unchanged in sgr/ (117, pre-existing) - the 24 errors mypy reports
  when checking startup_checks.py in isolation are all pre-existing
  findings in transitively imported modules (ccxt_base.py, event_bus.py,
  var_calculator.py, etc.), none originate in startup_checks.py itself.
